WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.610
- Hello, welcome to our
daily homeroom livestream

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.380
for those of y'all who are new to this.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.130
This is a live stream that

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.900
we're doing every day as the name implies,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.520
to keep us connected and answer questions

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.810
and figure out ways to
support each other during

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.960
these times of school closures.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.190
It's also a forum for you to ask me

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.580
and our guests questions,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.150
and we're gonna have a really
interesting guest today.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.770
I will remind folks Khan Academy

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.180
we are not for profit with a
mission of providing a free

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.360
world-class education for anyone anywhere,

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.100
and we're able to do the work we do

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.500
because of donations
from folks like yourself.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.790
So if you're in a position to do so,

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.920
please think about
donating to Khan Academy.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.700
I wanna give a special thanks
to several corporations

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.470
that have stepped up in the last few weeks

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.890
as we see it our Costco
hire, do the COVID crisis.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.030
We've seen our traffic
be almost three acts

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.370
of what it typically is.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.970
A special thanks to bank of America,

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.663
Google.org, Fastly, Novartis and AT&amp;T.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.950
So with that, I wanna get
right into the conversation,

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.120
I have a really great guest today

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.180
who's going to be able to
address a lot of concerns

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.490
that I think are out there.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.670
Lorraine Hastings is the vice president

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:09.720
with the College Board.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.110
For those of you all who are not familiar

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.990
with the College Board, the College Board

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:13.950
is a not for profit.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.740
We are partnered with the College Board.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:18.590
But the College Board also offers the SAT

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:22.060
and Lorraine specializes in relations

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.190
with college counselors, and
is an expert on all things

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.810
that are going on in the SAT right now.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.060
I know there's a lot of questions.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.250
And so first of all, Lorraine, welcome.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.100
Thank you for being here.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.000
I hope everything is good with your family

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.803
and this time of social distancing.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.370
Maybe a good place to start is you know,

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.730
what's the lay of the land for those of us

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.140
who haven't been fully keeping
track of what's going on

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.343
with the SAT with regards to COVID?

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.450
- Hi, Sal, thanks again for
the invitation to join today.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.520
I hope you and your
family are well as well

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.840
as your colleagues.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.480
The work you do at Khan Academy
could not be more important

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.730
as it is today,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:01.240
as we all learn to navigate
this difficult time.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:05.070
As the College Board responds
to the impact of Coronavirus.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.020
Our top priorities are the
health and safety of students

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.410
and educators.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.370
In face of school closures,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.050
we're adapting to give
students opportunities

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.770
to still show their strengths

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.250
and continue on the path to college.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.730
We're working hard to make
the SAT available in school

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.120
and out of school

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.170
as soon as the public
health situation allows.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:29.540
Right now public health
officials have made it clear

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.590
that it is not safe to
gather students in one place.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.470
Many states have closed school

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.160
for the rest of the school year,

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.120
and globally there is
widespread school closures

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.200
across 192 countries.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.360
Last week, we announced
that we will not be able

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.160
to administer the SAT as
planned on June sixth.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.120
If it's safe from a
public health standpoint,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.050
we will provide weekend SAT
administration's every month

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:00.920
beginning in August through
the end of the calendar year.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.270
This includes a new
administration in September,

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:07.850
and the previously scheduled
tests on August 29th,

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.420
October the third, November the seventh

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.470
and December the fifth.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:16.430
In the unlikely and I say
unlikely event that schools

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.743
do not reopen this fall,

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.630
we will provide a
digital SAT for home use.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.570
We of course would ensure
that at home SAT testing

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:32.020
is simple, secure, fair

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.950
and accessible to all
and most importantly,

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.860
valid for use in college admissions.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.100
I know that I've shared a few changes,

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.530
but Sal, even though it seems
as if everything is changing,

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.520
there is one thing that's not changing,

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.840
and that's the official
student practice available

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.310
for free anytime,

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.960
through our partnership with
you all at Khan Academy.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.140
- No, and this is super useful.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.590
And so just to make sure that I understand

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.670
what the College Board's
position on this is,

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.900
is as soon as we're through
this stay at home order,

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.325
y'all are going to
essentially offer the SAT

00:04:07.325 --> 00:04:09.180
on the regular schedule thereafter

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.890
and offer a few more.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.270
Hopefully you can kind of
view these as maybe makeup.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.530
So it's a monthly time period.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.680
And so is your view that
this will be sufficient

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.190
