00:24:33.090 --> 00:24:34.190
but I wanna re-answer it

00:24:34.190 --> 00:24:36.649
'cause I think it's
worth doubling down on.

00:24:36.649 --> 00:24:38.357
"Are SAT score going to count for anything

00:24:38.357 --> 00:24:41.077
"for next year college applications?"

00:24:42.490 --> 00:24:44.520
Lorraine, you wanna take a stab at it

00:24:44.520 --> 00:24:47.100
and I'm happy to answer it again.

00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:48.350
- So yeah, yeah.

00:24:48.350 --> 00:24:52.490
So once again, colleges are being flexible

00:24:52.490 --> 00:24:55.763
because they too understand
that there are some students

00:24:55.763 --> 00:24:58.340
who are applying this fall

00:24:58.340 --> 00:25:01.560
who won't have the
opportunity to take the test.

00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:04.780
So they're taking into
account these situations,

00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:09.270
but students should always
reach out to the college.

00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:11.140
If you can take the SAT,

00:25:11.140 --> 00:25:16.140
you should absolutely take
the SAT because once again,

00:25:16.480 --> 00:25:18.740
with the portfolio that
you have in addition

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:20.870
to your high school grade point average,

00:25:20.870 --> 00:25:22.590
your extracurricular activities,

00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:26.220
and whatever volunteer activities
that you're submitting,

00:25:26.220 --> 00:25:30.770
SAT scores will help
colleges show the skills.

00:25:30.770 --> 00:25:34.300
Some students and unfortunately,
Sal, when students

00:25:34.300 --> 00:25:37.360
sometimes hear that a
school is test optional

00:25:37.360 --> 00:25:39.390
or SAT optional, they feel oh,

00:25:39.390 --> 00:25:41.080
I don't have to take the test.

00:25:41.080 --> 00:25:43.190
And sometimes the more privileged students

00:25:43.190 --> 00:25:46.060
still take it, still submit those scores.

00:25:46.060 --> 00:25:48.470
And it's more of the underserved students

00:25:48.470 --> 00:25:52.070
who don't have a counselor
coaching them to say,

00:25:52.070 --> 00:25:54.530
go ahead, take the SAT regardless,

00:25:54.530 --> 00:25:58.310
even if it's test optional,
take it and submit it.

00:25:58.310 --> 00:26:00.170
So we really encourage you.

00:26:00.170 --> 00:26:01.580
If you can take it,

00:26:01.580 --> 00:26:03.670
please take it because it will do nothing

00:26:03.670 --> 00:26:07.990
but help your portfolio and
show a better presentation

00:26:07.990 --> 00:26:11.270
of yourself to that
college admissions officer.

00:26:11.270 --> 00:26:12.430
- And I'll just add to that,

00:26:12.430 --> 00:26:14.880
it's absolutely true that
everyone is more understanding

00:26:14.880 --> 00:26:15.960
and flexible right now,

00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:18.230
especially as we go into next
year's college admissions.

00:26:18.230 --> 00:26:20.340
But I know that a lot
of school districts have

00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:23.770
had to do things like go to
pass fail on their letter grades

00:26:23.770 --> 00:26:25.400
in this in this current semester

00:26:25.400 --> 00:26:26.600
because of the school closures.

00:26:26.600 --> 00:26:29.340
And so that gives even less
information for colleges

00:26:29.340 --> 00:26:30.710
to make their admissions decisions

00:26:30.710 --> 00:26:33.230
and so that you can imagine,
it might if you can,

00:26:33.230 --> 00:26:34.820
if you're in a position
to do so it's it might

00:26:34.820 --> 00:26:37.470
be even more valuable
to provide those signals

00:26:37.470 --> 00:26:40.550
of your your college readiness.

00:26:40.550 --> 00:26:43.150
And testing, I've talked to
college admissions officers

00:26:43.150 --> 00:26:46.110
of some fairly selective schools
that went testing optional,

00:26:46.110 --> 00:26:47.900
but what they'll tell you is that still

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:50.350
a disproportionate number
of the kids who get in

00:26:50.350 --> 00:26:51.430
did take the SAT

00:26:51.430 --> 00:26:52.990
because they still need to look

00:26:52.990 --> 00:26:54.690
at that they need some form of a signal.

00:26:54.690 --> 00:26:56.880
If you don't have something
like an SAT score,

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:59.420
you're still going to have to
have some other kind of signal

00:26:59.420 --> 00:27:02.340
to the college around
your college readiness

00:27:02.340 --> 00:27:05.140
and how it actually might
compare relative to other folks.

00:27:05.140 --> 00:27:08.130
So high;y, highly recommend
that if you're in a position

00:27:08.130 --> 00:27:10.940
to do so, highly recommend
to keep preparing.

